  Cell["Claim and proof", "Section"], Cell["Draft for human review. Partial \
result for Problem 1 research; not a solution\nto any prize problem. Not \
submitted to the Wolfram API.", "Text"], Cell["The exact claim is about the \
kit's sideways reconstruction, not the canonical\nsingle-seed center column. \
Begin with a period-four temporal column whose even\nentries are black and \
whose odd entries alternate white and black. Change\njust the white entry at \
time 8j+5 to black. The corresponding constrained start\nTheta(free j) is \
eventually periodic in space. Every eventual spatial period\nP>0 nevertheless \
satisfies j<2^P, whatever spatial transient is allowed.\nChoosing j=2^M \
therefore gives an explicit input for which every eventual\nspatial period \
exceeds M. The headline is\nRule30Submission.theta_explicit_large_periods.", 
   "Text"], Cell["Rule 30 updates a cell to left XOR (center OR right). The \
single-seed pattern\nand its center column motivate Prize Problem 1: does \
that column ever become\nperiodic? This essay does not answer it. It examines \
the complexity of an\nauxiliary reconstruction that appears in the open \
period-two reductions.", "Text"], Cell["Finite computations first gave \
spatial periods 7, 14 and 28. A period 56 example\nshowed that these were not \
an exhaustive catalogue. A symbolic lifting rule\nallows a spatial period to \
double when moving to an earlier temporal row.\nThe present argument explains \
why a bounded catalogue cannot suffice at all,\neven in a one-defect family \
satisfying four necessary finite word constraints.", "Text"], 
  Cell["Write pure(t)=[t mod 4 is not 1]. Its odd-time free input is 0, 1, 0, \
1, ... . In\nthe delayed family only free index 4j+2 is changed from 0 to 1, \
producing one\n111 run. Uniform Lean proofs show that the free input contains \
none of\n00, 11111, 010110 or 1011010. The construction is therefore more \
constrained than\nan arbitrary temporal word, while finite-right \
realizability remains open.", "Text"], Cell["The proof has four steps. First, \
a 312-cell reconstruction table proves that\nthe base defect's recurrent \
spatial tail differs from the pure periodic\nbackground. Second, outer \
locality preserves agreement beyond a finite\nspatial depth for every fixed \
elapsed time. Shifting two differently delayed\ninputs then shows that their \
reconstructed rows cannot agree on a spatial\ntail. Third, a row of eventual \
spatial period P has only 2^P possible residue\nwords, and any period of a \
later defect is inherited by all earlier defects.\nIf j>=2^P, pigeonhole \
would force two distinct delays to have the same tail.\nThus j<2^P. Finally, \
a finite temporal-profile argument proves that every\nmember really is \
eventually periodic in space; unboundedness is across the\nfamily, not \
nonperiodicity of an individual spatial row.", "Text"], 
  Cell["The notebook embeds its complete Lean source as an icon in the proof \
cell.\nIt obtains the kit path from RULE30PRIZE_KIT, uses LeanImportString to \
create\nrule30Submission, displays the headline types and axioms, and invokes \
the\nLeanLink full kernel check. It needs no local research files on a \
verifier.", "Text"], Cell["Validation before the notebook: a cold core build \
and full replay of all 173\ndeclarations passed at kit \
3eca23c0a9fa6b153313655e6d51835406c2d06e. After the\nverifier moved, the \
identical catalog source passed full replay \
at\n0090056412733accaa27643d3cbbf982104f2251 with no new axioms. The \
standalone\nRule30Submission source and the notebook receive separate checks \
recorded\nwith this draft. Lean 4.35.0 and the unchanged official checker are \
used.", "Text"], Cell["The unresolved questions are substantial. No member is \
proved to arise from\nan actual finite right half. No lower bound on spatial \
black density, no\ncritical-charge inequality, no absorption result and no \
canonical center\nnonperiodicity theorem follow. These statements cannot be \
promoted to a\nprize solution by observing more finite cases.", "Text"], 
  Cell["References: the official Rule30ZeroBoundary definitions, \
reconstruction,\nouter locality and Jen pigeonhole lemmas at the stated kit \
pin; the Rule30\nPrize Problem1 statement; and the full source in upstream \
PR25:\nhttps://github.com/WolframInstitute/Rule30PrizeKit/pull/25 . The \
separate\nperiod-lifting result is PR24. Both are proposed partial catalog \
contributions.", "Text"], Cell["The embedded formal proof", "Section"], 
  Cell[BoxData["Needs[\"Wolfram`LeanLink`\"];\n$Rule30PrizeKit = \
Environment[\"RULE30PRIZE_KIT\"];"], "Input"], 
  Cell[BoxData[RowBox[{"rule30Submission", "=", 
      RowBox[{"LeanImportString", "[", InterpretationBox[
         DynamicModuleBox[{Typeset`open = False}, TemplateBox[
           {"String", StyleBox["\"Lean source\"", "IconizedCustomName", 
             StripOnInput -> False], GridBox[{{RowBox[{TagBox["\"Head: \"", 
                  "IconizedLabel"], "\[InvisibleSpace]", TagBox["String", 
                  "IconizedItem"]}]}, {RowBox[{TagBox["\"String length: \"", 
                  "IconizedLabel"], "\[InvisibleSpace]", TagBox["23107", 
                  "IconizedItem"]}]}, {RowBox[{TagBox["\"Byte count: \"", 
                  "IconizedLabel"], "\[InvisibleSpace]", TagBox["24576", 
                  "IconizedItem"]}]}}, GridBoxAlignment -> {"Columns" -> 
                {{Left}}}, DefaultBaseStyle -> "Column", GridBoxItemSize -> 
              {"Columns" -> {{Automatic}}, "Rows" -> {{Automatic}}}], 
            Dynamic[Typeset`open]}, "IconizedObject"]], "import \
Ruliology.CellularAutomata.Rule30ZeroBoundary\nimport \
Ruliology.CellularAutomata.Rule30StripCertificates\n\n/-!\n# Delayed temporal \
defects force unbounded spatial tail periods\n\nLet `pure t = decide (t % 4 \
\[NotEqual] 1)`, the column whose even entries are black\nand whose free odd \
entries alternate 0,1. The family `input j` changes\nonly time `8*j+5` from \
white to black. Equivalently, its free sequence is\nalternating except for a \
black bit at index `4*j+2`, giving one run 111.\nThe free sequence avoids \
00,11111,010110 and 1011010, for every j.\n\nEvery `Theta (free j)` is a \
valid constrained start and is eventually\nperiodic in *space*. Nevertheless \
every eventual spatial period P>0\nsatisfies `j < 2^P` \
(`theta_delay_lt_pow_period`). Thus the explicit\nchoice j=2^M has no \
eventual period at most M, even with an arbitrary\nspatial transient \
(`theta_explicit_large_periods`).\n\nProof: a 312-cell table establishes the \
base defect's recurrent spatial\ntail, different from the pure background. \
Outer locality and temporal\nshift equivariance show that different delays \
have different tails modulo\nfinite prefixes. A P-periodic tail has at most \
2^P residue words. Periods\nare inherited by earlier delays, so j>=2^P would \
force a tail collision.\nTemporal periodicity gives eventual spatial \
periodicity by a separate\nfinite-profile argument, uniformly in the temporal \
preperiod.\n\nThese are synthetic temporal inputs, not proved finite-right \
responses or\nthe canonical single-seed center column. Each spatial member is \
periodic;\nthe periods across the family are unbounded. The result supplies \
no\ndensity bound, does not solve Q01 or CQ01, and solves no prize \
problem.\n\nContributed by Troy Lowry with OpenAI Codex, \
2026-10-25.\n-/\n\nnamespace Rule30Submission\nopen \
Ruliology.CellularAutomata\nopen Rule30ZeroBoundary \
Rule30StripCertificates\n\ndef TailEq (f g : Nat \[RightArrow] Bool) : Prop \
:= \[Exists] D, \[ForAll] d, D\[LessEqual]d \[RightArrow] f d=g d\n\ndef \
SpatialPeriod (P : Nat) (f : Nat \[RightArrow] Bool) : Prop :=\n  \[Exists] \
D, \[ForAll] d, D\[LessEqual]d \[RightArrow] f (d+P)=f d\n\ntheorem seg_eq (n \
: Nat) (f g : Nat \[RightArrow] Bool) (h : seg f n=seg g n) :\n    \[ForAll] \
i, i<n \[RightArrow] f i=g i := by\n  induction n generalizing f g with\n  | \
zero => intro i hi; omega\n  | succ n ih =>\n    change f 0 :: seg (fun i => \
f (i+1)) n = g 0 :: seg (fun i => g (i+1)) n at h\n    obtain \
\:27e8h0,ht\:27e9 := List.cons.inj h\n    intro i hi\n    cases i with\n    | \
zero => exact h0\n    | succ i => exact ih _ _ ht i (by omega)\n\ntheorem \
finite_bound (f : Nat \[RightArrow] Nat) (N : Nat) :\n    \[Exists] D, \
\[ForAll] j, j\[LessEqual]N \[RightArrow] f j\[LessEqual]D := by\n  induction \
N with\n  | zero =>\n    refine \:27e8f 0,fun j hj => ?_\:27e9\n    have h : \
j=0 := by omega\n    subst j\n    exact Nat.le_refl _\n  | succ N ih =>\n    \
obtain \:27e8D,hD\:27e9 := ih\n    refine \:27e8D+f (N+1),fun j hj => \
?_\:27e9\n    by_cases h : j\[LessEqual]N\n    \[CenterDot] have := hD j h; \
omega\n    \[CenterDot] have : j=N+1 := by omega\n      subst j; \
omega\n\ntheorem agree_from_window (f g : Nat \[RightArrow] Bool) (D P : Nat) \
(hP : 0<P)\n    (hf : \[ForAll] d, D\[LessEqual]d \[RightArrow] f (d+P)=f d) \
(hg : \[ForAll] d, D\[LessEqual]d \[RightArrow] g (d+P)=g d)\n    (hwin : seg \
(fun i => f (D+i)) P = seg (fun i => g (D+i)) P) : TailEq f g := by\n  have \
hall : \[ForAll] i, f (D+i)=g (D+i) := by\n    intro i\n    induction i using \
Nat.strongRecOn with\n    | ind i ih =>\n      by_cases hi : i<P\n      \
\[CenterDot] exact seg_eq P _ _ hwin i hi\n      \[CenterDot] rw [show \
D+i=(D+(i-P))+P by omega,hf _ (by omega),hg _ (by omega)]\n        exact ih \
(i-P) (by omega)\n  refine \:27e8D,fun d hd => ?_\:27e9\n  simpa [show \
D+(d-D)=d by omega] using hall (d-D)\n\n/-- Infinitely many distinct tail \
classes cannot share one eventual period. -/\ntheorem \
no_common_period_of_distinct (rows : Nat \[RightArrow] Nat \[RightArrow] \
Bool)\n    (hd : \[ForAll] m n, m<n \[RightArrow] \[Not]TailEq (rows m) (rows \
n)) (P : Nat) (hP : 0<P) :\n    \[Not]\[ForAll] j, SpatialPeriod P (rows j) \
:= by\n  intro hp\n  classical\n  let threshold (j : Nat) := Classical.choose \
(hp j)\n  have hthreshold (j : Nat) : \[ForAll] d, threshold j\[LessEqual]d \
\[RightArrow] rows j (d+P)=rows j d :=\n    Classical.choose_spec (hp j)\n  \
obtain \:27e8D,hD\:27e9 := finite_bound threshold (2^P)\n  let window (j : \
Nat) := seg (fun i => rows j (D+i)) P\n  obtain \:27e8m,n,hmn,hn,hwin\:27e9 \
:= Rule30Jen.pigeonhole P window\n    (fun j => length_seg P _)\n  apply hd m \
n hmn\n  exact agree_from_window _ _ D P hP\n    (fun d h => hthreshold m d \
(by have := hD m (by omega); omega))\n    (fun d h => hthreshold n d (by have \
:= hD n hn; omega)) hwin\n\ntheorem tail_recon_time {a b : Nat \[RightArrow] \
Bool}\n    (h : TailEq (fun d => recon a d 0) (fun d => recon b d 0)) (t : \
Nat) :\n    TailEq (fun d => recon a d t) (fun d => recon b d t) := by\n  \
obtain \:27e8D,hD\:27e9 := h\n  refine \:27e8D+1+t,fun d hd => ?_\:27e9\n  \
have hlocal := zrow_local (L:=lam a) (L':=lam b) (a:=D+1)\n    (by omega) \
(fun k hk => hD k (by omega)) t d hd\n  simpa only [zrow_lam] using \
hlocal\n\n\nopen Ruliology.CellularAutomata\nopen Rule30ZeroBoundary \
Rule30StripCertificates\n\ntheorem periodic_window_ext (T P : Nat) (hP : 0<P) \
(f g : Nat \[RightArrow] Bool)\n    (hf : \[ForAll] t, T\[LessEqual]t \
\[RightArrow] f (t+P)=f t) (hg : \[ForAll] t, T\[LessEqual]t \[RightArrow] g \
(t+P)=g t)\n    (hwin : \[ForAll] t, t<T+P \[RightArrow] f t=g t) : \[ForAll] \
t, f t=g t := by\n  intro t\n  induction t using Nat.strongRecOn with\n  | \
ind t ih =>\n    by_cases ht : t<T+P\n    \[CenterDot] exact hwin t ht\n    \
\[CenterDot] rw [show t=(t-P)+P by omega,hf _ (by omega),hg _ (by omega)]\n   \
   exact ih (t-P) (by omega)\n\ntheorem recon_time_period (a : Nat \
\[RightArrow] Bool) (T P : Nat)\n    (hper : \[ForAll] t, T\[LessEqual]t \
\[RightArrow] a (t+P)=a t) (d t : Nat) (ht : T\[LessEqual]t) :\n    recon a d \
(t+P)=recon a d t := by\n  rw [recon_shift]\n  apply recon_local\n  intro j \
hj\n  simpa [Nat.add_assoc] using hper (t+j) (by omega)\n\ndef profile (a : \
Nat \[RightArrow] Bool) (W d : Nat) :=\n  seg (fun i => if i<W then recon a d \
i else recon a (d+1) (i-W)) (2*W)\n\ntheorem profile_eq (a : Nat \
\[RightArrow] Bool) (T P : Nat) (hP : 0<P)\n    (hper : \[ForAll] t, \
T\[LessEqual]t \[RightArrow] a (t+P)=a t) (m n : Nat)\n    (h : profile a \
(T+P) m=profile a (T+P) n) :\n    (\[ForAll] t, recon a m t=recon a n t) \
\[And]\n    (\[ForAll] t, recon a (m+1) t=recon a (n+1) t) := by\n  have \
hfirst : \[ForAll] t, t<T+P \[RightArrow] recon a m t=recon a n t := by\n    \
intro t ht\n    have he := seg_eq (2*(T+P)) _ _ h t (by omega)\n    simpa \
only [ite_eq_left ht] using he\n  have hsecond : \[ForAll] t, t<T+P \
\[RightArrow] recon a (m+1) t=recon a (n+1) t := by\n    intro t ht\n    have \
he := seg_eq (2*(T+P)) _ _ h (T+P+t) (by omega)\n    simpa only [ite_eq_right \
(show \[Not]T+P+t<T+P by omega),Nat.add_sub_cancel_left] using he\n  exact \
\:27e8periodic_window_ext T P hP _ _ (recon_time_period a T P hper m)\n      \
(recon_time_period a T P hper n) hfirst,\n    periodic_window_ext T P hP _ _ \
(recon_time_period a T P hper (m+1))\n      (recon_time_period a T P hper \
(n+1)) hsecond\:27e9\n\n/-- An eventually periodic temporal input \
reconstructs an eventually\nperiodic spatial start. The bound may depend on \
the temporal transient. -/\ntheorem spatial_of_temporal (a : Nat \
\[RightArrow] Bool) (T P : Nat) (hP : 0<P)\n    (hper : \[ForAll] t, \
T\[LessEqual]t \[RightArrow] a (t+P)=a t) :\n    Rule30Jen.EventuallyPeriodic \
(fun d => recon a d 0) := by\n  obtain \:27e8m,n,hmn,hn,he\:27e9 := \
Rule30Jen.pigeonhole (2*(T+P)) (profile a (T+P))\n    (fun d => length_seg _ \
_)\n  have hpair := profile_eq a T P hP hper m n he\n  have key : \[ForAll] \
q, (\[ForAll] t, recon a (m+q) t=recon a (n+q) t) \[And]\n      (\[ForAll] t, \
recon a (m+q+1) t=recon a (n+q+1) t) := by\n    intro q\n    induction q \
with\n    | zero => simpa using hpair\n    | succ q ih =>\n      refine \
\:27e8?_,fun t => ?_\:27e9\n      \[CenterDot] simpa [Nat.add_assoc] using \
ih.2\n      \[CenterDot] rw [show m+(q+1)+1=m+q+2 by omega,\n          show \
n+(q+1)+1=n+q+2 by omega,recon_two,recon_two,ih.2,ih.2,ih.1]\n  refine \
\:27e8m,n-m,by omega,fun d hd => ?_\:27e9\n  have h := (key (d-m)).1 0\n  rw \
[show m+(d-m)=d by omega,show n+(d-m)=d+(n-m) by omega] at h\n  exact \
h.symm\n\n\nopen Ruliology.CellularAutomata\nopen Rule30ZeroBoundary\n\ndef \
columns : List (List Bool) := [\n  [false, false, false, false, false, false, \
false, false, false, false, false, false],\n  [true, false, true, true, true, \
true, true, true, true, false, true, true],\n  [true, true, false, false, \
false, false, false, false, true, true, false, false],\n  [false, true, true, \
true, true, true, true, false, false, true, true, false],\n  [false, false, \
false, false, false, false, true, false, false, false, true, false],\n  \
[false, true, true, true, true, false, true, false, false, false, true, \
false],\n  [true, false, false, false, true, true, true, false, false, true, \
true, false],\n  [true, true, true, false, false, false, true, false, true, \
false, true, false],\n  [false, false, true, false, true, false, true, true, \
